    "evidenceByGoal": "Adult growth hormone deficiency—body composition and related efficacy outcomes: Design: randomized, parallel 3-arm, placebo-controlled double-blind and active-controlled open-label trial. [449] Population/sample: 259 adults with growth hormone deficiency across 21 countries; participants were treatment-naive or had not received growth hormone in the prior year and were randomized 1:1:1 to lonapegsomatropin, weekly placebo, or daily somatropin. [449] Dose: fixed dosing based on age and oral estrogen intake; an exact lonapegsomatropin dose was not reported in the reviewed source. [449] Duration: 12-week titration followed by 26 weeks of fixed-dose treatment, with outcomes assessed at week 38. [449] Comparator: once-weekly placebo and daily somatropin. [449] Outcomes: lonapegsomatropin improved trunk percent fat versus placebo (LS mean difference −2.0%, p < 0.0001), total-body lean mass (LS mean difference 1.7 kg, p < 0.0001), and trunk fat mass (LS mean difference −0.7 kg, p = 0.0053) at week 38. [449] Adverse events: severe adverse events occurred in 3.4% with lonapegsomatropin, 1.2% with placebo, and 2.3% with daily somatropin; treatment-related adverse events occurred in 24.7% and 22.1% with lonapegsomatropin and daily somatropin, respectively. [449] Injection-site reactions occurred in 4.5% with lonapegsomatropin, 5.8% with daily somatropin, and 4.8% with placebo, and A1c levels remained stable in all arms. [449] Key limitation: not verified in reviewed source.\n\nPediatric growth hormone deficiency—growth efficacy: Design: randomized, open-label, active-controlled, 52-week, phase 3 trial. [450] Population/sample: treatment-naive, prepubertal Chinese children with growth hormone deficiency; 153 participants received treatment. [450] Dose: lonapegsomatropin 0.24 mg growth-hormone/kg/week versus daily somatropin 0.034 mg/kg/day. [450] Duration: 52 weeks. [450] Comparator: daily somatropin. [450] Outcome: annualized height velocity at week 52 was 10.66 ± 0.22 cm/year with weekly lonapegsomatropin versus 9.75 ± 0.26 cm/year with daily somatropin; the difference was 0.91 ± 0.28 cm/year (95% CI 0.37–1.45; p = 0.0010), and change in height standard deviation score also favored lonapegsomatropin. [450] Adverse events: the source reports similar safety profiles between treatment groups and comparable safety and tolerability, without event counts. [450] Key limitation: not verified in reviewed source.",
