    "latestVerifiedPublicationYear": 2001,
    "humanStudyCount": 2,
    "totalStudyCount": 3,
    "evidenceByGoal": "Serum hormone modulation: (1) Randomized, placebo-controlled, 28-day parallel-group study in healthy men aged 30–58 years (androstenediol 300 mg/day within a multi-ingredient supplement, n=28; placebo, n=27). Total testosterone and PSA were unchanged; serum androstenedione increased 174%, free testosterone 37%, DHT 57%, and estradiol 86%; HDL-C decreased by 0.14 mmol/L. Adverse events were not mentioned in the reviewed source. Key limitation: the effect cannot be attributed to androstenediol alone because the intervention also contained six herbal/nutritional ingredients. [475]\n\n(2) Randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled crossover study in eight experienced male weight lifters aged 22.9 ± 1.2 years; 20 mg sublingual cyclodextrin-androstenediol versus placebo, with blood sampling for 3 hours after intake and at least 1 week between treatments. Compared with placebo, androstenedione increased from 60–180 minutes and peaked 125% above baseline at 150 minutes, free testosterone increased from 30–180 minutes and peaked 118% above baseline at 60 minutes, and estradiol increased from 30–180 minutes and peaked 71% above baseline at 180 minutes. Adverse events were not mentioned in the reviewed source. Key limitation: very small sample, acute follow-up, and a sublingual cyclodextrin formulation that should not be generalized to other formulations. [477]\n\nThe 4-hydroxyandrostenedione record was excluded as an identity mismatch and was not used as evidence for 4-androstenediol. [483]",
